scotty (tcl-tnm) for Debian
===========================

Why this package exists
-----------------------
ritz needs the Tnm Tcl extension ("package require Tnm"). Tnm used to reach
Debian via the `scotty` package, but scotty was orphaned and removed from the
archive long ago. This source package rebuilds Tnm from the actively-
maintained FlightAware fork of scotty, as the binary package tcl-tnm, so ritz
(and anything else needing Tnm) has a dependency to point at.

Build notes / gotchas
---------------------
The upstream build is TEA/autoconf and predates modern toolchains. The
packaging works around several issues; if you bump the upstream version,
re-check these:

  * configure.ac ships without a generated configure, so debian/rules runs
    autoheader + autoconf by hand (not autoreconf -fi, which would clobber
    the bundled TEA macros in aclocal.m4).

  * Built against libtirpc (--with-tirpc); modern glibc no longer provides
    SUN RPC. rpcgen comes from the rpcsvc-proto build-dependency.

  * The SUN RPC stub objects (*_clnt.o / *_xdr.o) are referenced by the link
    line but are not in PKG_OBJECTS, and make does not track rpcgen's
    side-effect outputs. debian/rules pre-generates and compiles them.

  * patches/0001 drops $(PKG_LIBS) from the shared library's Make
    prerequisites (it carries -L flags under --with-tirpc).

  * GCC 14+ legacy-C errors are demoted to warnings via
    DEB_CFLAGS_MAINT_APPEND.

Where things install
--------------------
The Tcl package lands in /usr/lib/tcltk/<multiarch>/Tnm<version>/, which is on
Tcl's auto_path, so "package require Tnm" finds it without TCLLIBPATH. (The
bare multiarch libdir that dh defaults to is NOT on auto_path, hence the
explicit --libdir.) The build also produces a standalone scotty interpreter
and nmtrapd/nmicmpd daemons; ritz does not need them, so debian/rules removes
them (along with the section-n Tcl API man pages) before packaging.

A note on 64-bit
----------------
Upstream documents known bugs in scotty's SNMP and frozen-MIB code paths on
64-bit platforms. ritz only uses Tnm's MIB symbol translation, which works
correctly; heavy live-SNMP use of this build on 64-bit is not guaranteed.

 -- Morten Brekkevold <morten.brekkevold@sikt.no>
